  "id": "COMPOUND:12251 - PROTEIN:586",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex, multi-step relationship between Magnesium levulinate and Retinal dehydrogenase 2, mediated through Selgantolimod. All three paths indicate that Magnesium levulinate acts as a target for Selgantolimod, which in turn targets Retinal dehydrogenase 2. This suggests that Selgantolimod may function as a modulator or inhibitor of Retinal dehydrogenase 2, potentially affecting retinal function. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The presence of multiple targets (Complement C1s subcomponent, HLA class I histocompatibility antigen, and Apolipoprotein B receptor) suggests that Selgantolimod may have diverse biological effects, possibly through different pathways. The integration of these findings highlights the role of Selgantolimod as a central mediator in the interaction between Magnesium levulinate and Retinal dehydrogenase 2, though further investigation is needed to elucidate the precise molecular mechanisms involved.",
